From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julia Lavrova <jlavrova@google.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 21:48:13 +0000
Subject: Fix integer overflow and oversized glyph rasterization in SDF
 generation

Skip prepareForImage in RemoteStrike::writePendingGlyphs and guard the
setImageHasBeenCalled assert in SkGlyph::flattenImage when a glyph
exceeds atlas dimensions so oversized glyphs are not rasterized into
discarded buffers. Validate positive dimensions and check that the
padded distance field and 17-byte-per-pixel scratch buffers fit in int
in SkComputeDistanceFieldSize and SkDistanceFieldGen, reject oversized
masks upfront in SDFMaskFilterImpl::filterMask, switch temporary
allocations to canfail variants, and free the destination image when
SDFMaskFilter fails.

Testing:
- Without the fix, rendering the HTML/font reproducer in Chromium calls
  SkGenerateDistanceFieldFromA8Image(4071, 65527) and aborts in
  sk_out_of_memory(); with the fix, the oversized glyph falls back to a
  path without entering SkGenerateDistanceFieldFromA8Image.
- DistanceFieldTest exercises A8, LCD16, and BW distance field
  generation and SkComputeDistanceFieldBufferSize at the exact
  INT_MAX / 17 (126,322,560 pixels: 10927x11540 vs 10928x11540)
  overflow boundary, non-positive dimensions, and SDFMaskFilter bounds
  overflow.
- SkRemoteGlyphCache_b576664769 tests SkStrikeServer to SkStrikeClient
  serialization of a font with an oversized hmtx advance and zero-contour
  glyf entries under both FreeType (dm) and Fontations (dm --fontations).
- Verified on 32-bit (x86) and 64-bit (x86_64 ASAN) Linux and Windows
  trybots, Canary-Android, and Canary-Chromium.

Bug: b/576664769
